<td id="S5.T5.6.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1.7pt 8.0pt;"><span id="S5.T5.6.3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">86.0</span></td>
</tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experiments on Scientific Domain.</span> It can be observed from Table <a href="#S5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 5.2.2 Results of Domain Teacher Training ‣ 5.2 Results and Observations ‣ 5 Experimental Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> that the science-enhanced teacher displays a comprehensive superiority compared with the baseline Qwen3.5-35B-A3B, especially on FS-R. It demonstrates that the proposed two-stage SFT can significantly promote both the intrinsic reasoning ability and extrinsic tool-use interaction capability in scientific scenarios.</p>
</div>
